From 717896c54d21c9953e3a1ceccf33073aca718a42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:16:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(example): give the editor backstage the start page data

The editor configuration now carries what the File menu of the editor
shows like Word does:

- templates: the start page templates of the same document type, with
  their thumbnails and a /elixir/new link (falls back to the upstream
  "Blank / With sample content" pair);
- recent: the stored files, newest first (name, editor link, location,
  modification date, size);
- elixir: host URLs used by the editor pages (start page, upload,
  editor link pattern, share link of the document, storage name,
  extensions the upload can open directly).

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
